case-organizer (4.6) stable; urgency=high

  * Added the Calendar / court-event tracker (/calendar): per-case hearing
    and listing dates (with purpose), filing deadlines (mark-filed with the
    actual filing date), appearance records (who appeared — team members or
    outside counsel by name), and other deadlines such as limitation
    periods. The page scales to the full viewport (month rows stretch to
    fill the screen height with equal top/bottom gaps) with type-coloured
    chips and overdue markers. A resizable full-height sidebar — position
    (left/right) and width persisted per browser — holds the per-day agenda
    (listed / due / filed / appeared) and a per-case timeline reachable by
    the same case-name search as Manage Case or by year/month browsing
    (deep-linkable via /calendar?year=&month=&case=). The "Record
    Appearance" flow captures who appeared and the outcome, and taking a
    next date auto-creates the linked next hearing. Case pickers in the
    event and appearance dialogs also offer search-by-name. Dates in the
    dialogs use the Indian dd/mm/yyyy format — typed digits auto-format
    and a calendar button opens the native date picker. Navigation lives
    in the account menu; the home page is unchanged.
  * Daily digest email: every morning (default 07:00, configurable under
    Settings -> System -> Daily Digest) active admins and users receive
    today's listings, filings due, overdue unfiled items, and tomorrow's
    matters; events can be assigned to users, who get an "ASSIGNED TO YOU"
    section. Sent by an in-process scheduler thread with a reminder_log
    claim so restarts never double-send; a "Send test digest now" button
    verifies SMTP without waiting. Interns never receive the digest.
  * Schema migration v7 -> v8: new case_events, event_participants,
    event_assignees, and reminder_log tables. Events reference cases by
    their year/month/name folder triple; the rename-case and delete-item
    endpoints now cascade so events follow renamed cases and are removed
    with deleted ones.
  * Interns get view-only calendar access: the page and read APIs are
    allowed, all event writes remain blocked.
  * Court-data auto-sync (eCourts/SCI/DHC) was researched and deliberately
    left out: no free official API exists for practitioners (see
    CALENDAR_PLAN.md for the research summary and options).
  * Legal notice generator: the recipient block no longer ends with a
    dangling comma — continuation commas are now placed on every line
    except the last (previously, when no contact was given, the final
    address line carried a trailing comma).
  * Admin Settings: new "Records" tab with "Delete Legal Notice Entries"
    and "Delete Internship Certificate Entries" tables. Each card carries a
    red info icon whose hover tooltip explains that deletion also removes
    the stored PDF (copies added into case folders are left untouched), and
    every delete asks for confirmation. Backed by admin-only
    DELETE /api/legal-notices/<id> and /api/certificates/<id> endpoints.
  * Added CALENDAR_PLAN.md — the approved implementation plan for the
    upcoming calendar / court-event tracker / daily digest system.
  * Fixed the first-request bootstrap hook closing the app-context database
    connection mid-request; the connection is now left to the standard
    teardown, removing a latent double-open per first request.
  * Tests: added tests/test_calendar.py (event CRUD, agenda/timeline
    queries, appearance composite, rename/delete cascades, intern
    read-only enforcement, digest content and idempotency, scheduler) and
    tests/test_records.py (recipient block commas, record deletion
    endpoints, permission checks); suite now 223 tests.

