case-organizer (4.5.3) stable; urgency=medium

  * Added a third user role, "intern", alongside admin and user. Interns may
    reach only the home page, My Account, internal Mail, and the PDF (bento)
    editing tools; every other feature is blocked. Enforcement is a
    default-deny before_request allowlist (_restrict_interns), so any route
    not explicitly listed is off-limits to interns. The account menu and the
    home page hide the restricted tools for interns, showing a simple
    landing instead.
  * Schema migration v6 -> v7: the users.role CHECK constraint was widened to
    accept 'intern' via a data-preserving table rebuild — existing users,
    roles, and active sessions are unchanged. The admin Settings user
    create/edit forms gained an "Intern" option.
  * PDF tools (BentoPDF) now follow the app's light/dark theme instead of
    always rendering dark. Light-mode overrides remap bento's custom gray
    palette variables and the component classes that hardcode Tailwind's
    default hex (tool cards, category filters, panels, pills, shortcut keys,
    etc.), scoped to the tool shell and to light mode; dark mode is
    unchanged. The self-themed markdown editor is left as-is.
  * Refactor: the account dropdown menu, previously duplicated across 11
    templates, was extracted into a shared templates/_user_menu.html partial.
  * Tests: added tests/test_intern.py (intern access allow/deny, role
    validation, admin/user unaffected); suite now 174 tests.

