case-organizer (4.5) stable; urgency=high

  * Added Legal Notice module: new /legal-notice page to upload a notice
    PDF and stamp it with a stored letterhead plus a recipient/notice
    header band (recipient, relation, address, contact). Auto-numbered
    N/LN/YY with yearly reset, stored under FS_ROOT with metadata in the
    new `legal_notices` DB table (schema migration v4 -> v5).
  * Added Legal Notice, Certificate, Letterhead, and Vakalatnama cards
    and links to the homepage and user menus across all pages.
  * Reworked the Settings page into a tabbed layout covering user
    management, SMTP configuration, and the letterhead and vakalatnama
    libraries.
  * Invoice form: letterhead picker with live preview improvements.
  * Search results: right-clicking a case now opens the same action
    menu as the three-line button (Manage Case, and for admins Edit
    Case Name / Delete Case), positioned at the cursor and clamped to
    the viewport; right-clicking elsewhere dismisses it.
  * Vendored Quill editor assets under static/vendor/quill (no CDN
    dependency).
  * Security: /logout is now POST-only with CSRF protection; the topbar
    logout link was converted to a styled form so third-party pages can
    no longer force-logout users via <img src="/logout">.
  * Security: login latency no longer reveals whether an email address
    is registered — a reference Argon2 verification always runs.
  * Security: session tokens are stored as SHA-256 hashes (DB schema
    migration v5 → v6, column renamed session_token → session_token_hash).
    Existing tokens are hashed in place, so active logins are preserved.
  * Security: main-app Content-Security-Policy is now nonce-based —
    'unsafe-inline' and 'unsafe-eval' were removed from script-src and
    every inline script carries a per-request nonce. Inline onclick
    handlers were replaced with CSP-safe data-confirm attributes.
  * Security: Bento CSP narrowed (default-src 'self'); new env var
    CASEORG_BENTO_CDN=0 strips the cdn.jsdelivr.net origin entirely for
    deployments that self-host the optional WASM engines.
  * Security: case-law FTS5 search input is fully sanitised — terms are
    quoted so FTS5 operator syntax (*, ^, :, NEAR()) cannot be injected;
    query length capped at 500 chars, NEAR distance at 50; malformed
    expressions can no longer 500 the search endpoint.
  * Security: uniform password policy on /setup, /reset-password,
    /account, and admin user creation: minimum stays at 8 characters
    (compatible with existing passwords), new 128-character maximum
    prevents Argon2 CPU exhaustion via multi-MB passwords.
  * Security: password reset tokens are compared with
    secrets.compare_digest() instead of SQL string equality.
  * Security: error responses no longer leak internal paths or
    exception details; full errors go to the server log instead.
  * Security: CSRF failures redirect to the home page instead of the
    client-controlled request URL (open redirect fix).
  * Security: uploads reject masked double extensions (e.g.
    report.html.txt) and txt/json content that is actually HTML/SVG.
    Filenames with ordinary dots ("State v. Sharma.pdf") still work.
  * Security: OCR language codes validated against a strict pattern
    before being passed to Tesseract; ZIP exports capped at 500 MB.
  * New env var CASEORG_COOKIE_SECURE: session cookies are Secure
    (HTTPS-only) by default in production; set CASEORG_COOKIE_SECURE=0
    for plain-HTTP LAN deployments without TLS, otherwise browsers will
    not send the session cookie and login cannot work.
  * Security: X-XSS-Protection set to "0" (deprecated auditor disabled;
    CSP is the XSS mitigation), Argon2 parameters pinned explicitly,
    PBKDF2 default raised to 600k iterations (new installs only —
    existing installs keep their stored iteration count), PDF job IDs
    raised to 256-bit entropy, master.key chmod failures now log a
    warning instead of being silently ignored.
  * DB schema migration v5 -> v6: user_sessions.session_token renamed to
    session_token_hash with existing tokens hashed in place.
  * Expanded test suite from 98 to 132 tests: schema v5->v6 upgrade with
    live sessions, CSP nonce coverage of every authenticated page, FTS5
    sanitisation, upload validation, timing-oracle mitigation, rate-limit
    proxy trust, settings/PBKDF2/Argon2 hardening, and env-var override
    behaviour (tests/test_config_env.py).
  * debian: Recommend ttf-mscorefonts-installer so certificate PDFs can
    render in genuine Times New Roman.

