case-organizer (4.3) stable; urgency=high

  * Security: added _safe_path() traversal checks to all routes that
    construct filesystem paths from user input (api_months, api_cases,
    create_case, manage_case_upload, api_update_note, api_note,
    _invoice_target_path).
  * Security: replaced hardcoded SECRET_KEY fallback with ephemeral
    secrets.token_urlsafe(32); app raises RuntimeError if no key is
    configured.
  * Security: added explicit @require_login / @require_login_api
    decorators to all routes that previously relied solely on the
    global setup hook (defense-in-depth).
  * Security: fixed rate-limit bypass via X-Forwarded-For spoofing;
    _get_client_ip() now trusts proxy hops only when
    CASEORG_TRUSTED_PROXY is set.
  * Security: set SESSION_COOKIE_SECURE in production and added HSTS
    header (Strict-Transport-Security) when not in debug mode.
  * Added POST /api/rename-case endpoint (admin-only) with _safe_path
    validation on both source and target, path separator rejection,
    depth guard, and conflict check.
  * Replaced browser prompt() for case renaming with custom blur-overlay
    modal dialog (Escape / click-outside to cancel).
  * Replaced per-case hamburger + trash buttons with a unified dropdown
    action menu (Manage Case, Edit Case Name, Delete Case) positioned
    via getBoundingClientRect() to avoid container clipping.
  * Repositioned date field in Create Case form to align with Case Name
    preview row, pairing petitioner/respondent fields symmetrically.
  * Unified tab selector styling (Manage Case and Search Case Law) into
    a consistent segmented control with auto-width columns.
  * Made Upload Case Law citation input heights uniform with standard
    form fields.
  * Removed redundant "We're Representing:" label from Create Case form.
  * Fixed case-law SQLite "database is locked" errors on SMB/CIFS mounts
    by moving schema initialisation to startup, adding busy_timeout, and
    skipping schema setup when tables already exist.
  * Fixed login box vertical centering regression.

